  ('corporate', 'Corporate.', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'validators-staking-providers', NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"extras": {"- Runs validator infrastructure at scale\n- Coordinates and operates staked ETH\n- Directly participates in block proposal and attestation": "- Runs validators at scale\n- Custodies and coordinates large amounts of staked ETH\n- Materially impacts validator concentration", "Client- or custodian-controlled keys with operational signing coordination (HSM / institutional custody integrations).": "Custodian-controlled keys.", "Delegated, non-custodial (institutional staking-as-a-service).": "Pooled, custodial staking.", "Enterprise validator operator providing staking infrastructure for institutions and funds.": "Large-scale custodial staking provider operating Ethereum validators for pooled ETH.", "Enterprise-grade validator operator running Ethereum validators for institutions, custodians, and asset managers.": "Large-scale validator operator for ETH staked through Binance’s custodial staking offerings.", "Figment": "Binance (Validator Operations)", "Figment is often the default choice for regulated entities entering ETH staking, which makes it disproportionately influential despite not being the largest operator.": "Binance’s validator operations amplify correlated risk due to scale, client concentration, and infrastructure centralization.", "Geth, Nethermind.": "Geth.", "Hybrid (self-managed infra with controlled cloud usage and redundancy).": "Cloud-heavy, scale-optimized infrastructure.", "If Figment disappeared, a meaningful amount of institutional ETH would stop validating or require rapid migration.": "If Binance’s validator infrastructure were removed, a large volume of ETH would immediately stop validating.", "Lighthouse, Teku (institution-favored, diversity-conscious).": "Prysm (historically dominant), Lighthouse.", "Medium (actively managed for diversity).": "High (large scale + client homogeneity).", "Medium (institutional jurisdictions, but geographically distributed).": "Medium–High (global footprint but centralized operational control).", "Medium (material institutional share, not dominant).": "Large.", "Medium.": "High.", "Professional Validator Operator": "Staking-as-a-Service Provider", "https://figment.io": "https://www.binance.com/en/eth-staking"}, "source_label": "Validators & Staking Providers"}'::jsonb),
  ('dao-governed-lido-dao-sets-operator-selection-incentives-and-policies', 'DAO-governed (Lido DAO sets operator selection, incentives, and policies).', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'validators-staking-providers', NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"extras": {"- Runs validator infrastructure at scale\n- Coordinates and operates staked ETH\n- Directly participates in block proposal and attestation": "- ETH deposited into Lido is actively staked via node operators\n- Protocol directly converts pooled ETH into live validators\n- Operator selection and coordination are essential for validation", "Client- or custodian-controlled keys with operational signing coordination (HSM / institutional custody integrations).": "Operator-managed keys with protocol governance constraints; increasing adoption of distributed validator technology (DVT).", "Delegated, non-custodial (institutional staking-as-a-service).": "Protocol-coordinated, delegated, non-custodial (ETH pooled into protocol; validators run by approved operators).", "Enterprise validator operator providing staking infrastructure for institutions and funds.": "Protocol-coordinated validator infrastructure operated by a decentralized set of professional node operators on behalf of pooled ETH.", "Enterprise-grade validator operator running Ethereum validators for institutions, custodians, and asset managers.": "Coordinates a decentralized set of professional node operators to run Ethereum validators for ETH deposited into the Lido protocol.", "Figment": "Lido (Node Operator Set)", "Figment is often the default choice for regulated entities entering ETH staking, which makes it disproportionately influential despite not being the largest operator.": "Lido is the single largest source of liquid-staked ETH, making its operator set one of the most systemically important validator groupings despite internal decentralization.", "Geth, Nethermind.": "Geth, Nethermind, Besu (diversity-aware rotation).", "Hybrid (self-managed infra with controlled cloud usage and redundancy).": "Hybrid and operator-distributed (multiple independent operators with heterogeneous infra).", "If Figment disappeared, a meaningful amount of institutional ETH would stop validating or require rapid migration.": "Without Lido’s operator coordination, a significant portion of ETH would immediately stop validating.", "Lighthouse, Teku (institution-favored, diversity-conscious).": "Lighthouse, Teku, Prysm (explicitly managed for diversity).", "Medium (actively managed for diversity).": "Medium (managed diversity, but scale introduces correlation).", "Medium (institutional jurisdictions, but geographically distributed).": "Medium (operator diversity offsets protocol-level concentration).", "Medium (material institutional share, not dominant).": "Large.", "Medium.": "High.", "Professional Validator Operator": "Liquid Staking Protocol Operators (Infrastructure Side)", "https://figment.io": "https://lido.fi"}, "source_label": "Validators & Staking Providers"}'::jsonb),
  ('protocol-embedded-dao-governance-governs-parameters-not-operators', 'Protocol-embedded + DAO (governance governs parameters, not operators).', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'validators-staking-providers', NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"extras": {"- Runs validator infrastructure at scale\n- Coordinates and operates staked ETH\n- Directly participates in block proposal and attestation": "- Directly enables ETH to be converted into validators\n- Coordinates rETH staking into active validation\n- Expands validator participation beyond professional operators", "Client- or custodian-controlled keys with operational signing coordination (HSM / institutional custody integrations).": "Operator-controlled keys with protocol-enforced collateral and slashing incentives.", "Delegated, non-custodial (institutional staking-as-a-service).": "Permissionless, protocol-coordinated, non-custodial.", "Enterprise validator operator providing staking infrastructure for institutions and funds.": "Permissionless protocol enabling independent operators to run Ethereum validators using pooled ETH.", "Enterprise-grade validator operator running Ethereum validators for institutions, custodians, and asset managers.": "Decentralized liquid staking protocol that enables permissionless validator operation through independent node operators.", "Figment": "Rocket Pool (Node Operators)", "Figment is often the default choice for regulated entities entering ETH staking, which makes it disproportionately influential despite not being the largest operator.": "Rocket Pool is structurally important for decentralization even with a smaller validator share, as it reduces reliance on large professional operators.", "Geth, Nethermind.": "Geth, Nethermind (operator-selected).", "Hybrid (self-managed infra with controlled cloud usage and redundancy).": "Highly decentralized (independent operators with heterogeneous infra).", "If Figment disappeared, a meaningful amount of institutional ETH would stop validating or require rapid migration.": "Rocket Pool directly converts ETH into validators; removal would reduce decentralized participation.", "Lighthouse, Teku (institution-favored, diversity-conscious).": "Lighthouse, Nimbus, Teku (operator-selected, diversity-friendly).", "Medium (actively managed for diversity).": "Low.", "Medium (institutional jurisdictions, but geographically distributed).": "Low.", "Medium (material institutional share, not dominant).": "Small–Medium.", "Medium.": "Low.", "Professional Validator Operator": "Liquid Staking Protocol Operators (Infrastructure Side)", "https://figment.io": "https://rocketpool.net"}, "source_label": "Validators & Staking Providers"}'::jsonb),
  ('protocol-governed-on-chain-governance-and-operator-selection', 'Protocol-governed (on-chain governance and operator selection).', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'validators-staking-providers', NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"extras": {"- Runs validator infrastructure at scale\n- Coordinates and operates staked ETH\n- Directly participates in block proposal and attestation": "- Runs validator infrastructure through operator coordination\n- ETH deposited into the protocol is actively staked\n- Protocol decisions directly affect validator operation", "Client- or custodian-controlled keys with operational signing coordination (HSM / institutional custody integrations).": "Operator-managed keys with protocol governance and incentive alignment.", "Delegated, non-custodial (institutional staking-as-a-service).": "Protocol-coordinated, operator-managed staking.", "Enterprise validator operator providing staking infrastructure for institutions and funds.": "Liquid staking protocol coordinating operator-managed Ethereum validators for pooled ETH.", "Enterprise-grade validator operator running Ethereum validators for institutions, custodians, and asset managers.": "Liquid staking protocol operating Ethereum validators through coordinated node operators.", "Figment": "StakeWise (Operator Infrastructure)", "Figment is often the default choice for regulated entities entering ETH staking, which makes it disproportionately influential despite not being the largest operator.": "StakeWise sits between Lido and Rocket Pool in decentralization, offering protocol coordination with a smaller but meaningful validator footprint.", "Geth, Nethermind.": "Geth.", "Hybrid (self-managed infra with controlled cloud usage and redundancy).": "Hybrid (operator-run infra coordinated through protocol).", "If Figment disappeared, a meaningful amount of institutional ETH would stop validating or require rapid migration.": "ETH deposited into StakeWise would not be validating without its operator infrastructure and coordination.", "Lighthouse, Teku (institution-favored, diversity-conscious).": "Lighthouse, Teku.", "Medium (actively managed for diversity).": "Medium.", "Medium (institutional jurisdictions, but geographically distributed).": "Medium.", "Medium (material institutional share, not dominant).": "Small.", "Medium.": "Low–Medium.", "Professional Validator Operator": "Liquid Staking Protocol Operators (Infrastructure Side)", "https://figment.io": "https://stakewise.io"}, "source_label": "Validators & Staking Providers"}'::jsonb),
  ('individual-diffuse-non-coordinated', 'Individual (diffuse, non-coordinated).', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'validators-staking-providers', NULL, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"extras": {"- Runs validator infrastructure at scale\n- Coordinates and operates staked ETH\n- Directly participates in block proposal and attestation": "Solo validators are not operationally efficient at scale, but they are structurally irreplaceable. They anchor Ethereum’s decentralization assumptions and reduce correlated failure risk.", "Client- or custodian-controlled keys with operational signing coordination (HSM / institutional custody integrations).": "User-controlled keys (local signing, often hardware-backed).", "Delegated, non-custodial (institutional staking-as-a-service).": "Solo, non-custodial, self-operated.", "Enterprise validator operator providing staking infrastructure for institutions and funds.": "Independent individuals running Ethereum validators using their own ETH and hardware.", "Enterprise-grade validator operator running Ethereum validators for institutions, custodians, and asset managers.": "- Run validator infrastructure directly\n- Propose and attest blocks independently\n- Provide decentralization, censorship resistance, and client diversity", "Figment": "Solo Validators", "Figment is often the default choice for regulated entities entering ETH staking, which makes it disproportionately influential despite not being the largest operator.": "- Not a single entity\n- Collectively critical for decentralization", "Geth, Nethermind.": "Highly diverse (Geth, Nethermind, Erigon).", "Hybrid (self-managed infra with controlled cloud usage and redundancy).": "Fully self-hosted or lightly cloud-assisted (home setups, small VPS, hybrid).", "If Figment disappeared, a meaningful amount of institutional ETH would stop validating or require rapid migration.": "Removing solo validators would materially reduce censorship resistance, client diversity, and the credibility of Ethereum’s decentralization guarantees.", "Lighthouse, Teku (institution-favored, diversity-conscious).": "Highly diverse (Lighthouse, Nimbus, Teku, Prysm).", "Medium (actively managed for diversity).": "Low (maximal heterogeneity).", "Medium (institutional jurisdictions, but geographically distributed).": "Low.", "Medium (material institutional share, not dominant).": "Medium (material but fragmented).", "Medium.": "Low.", "Professional Validator Operator": "Solo Validators (Aggregated Category)", "https://figment.io": "N/A (individual operators)"}, "source_label": "Validators & Staking Providers"}'::jsonb),
  ('flashbots-block-builder', 'Flashbots (Block Builder)', 'core-protocol-architecture', 'mev-block-builders', 'https://www.flashbots.net/', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Flashbots operates one of the most influential Ethereum block builders, historically shaping how MEV is extracted and how builders interface with validators.", "extras": {"Block Construction Authority": "Full (constructs complete blocks)", "Censorship or Filtering Policies": "Historically OFAC-aligned at the relay level; evolving policies", "Estimated Validator Coverage": "Large (historically dominant share of builder-supplied blocks)", "Governance Influence Vector": "Corporate + Ecosystem (de facto standards influence)", "Infrastructure Control": "Centralized (single primary builder stack)", "MEV Subsector Type": "Block Builder", "Operational Role": "Constructs Ethereum blocks by ordering transactions and MEV bundles, submitting blocks to validators primarily via relay infrastructure.", "Practitioner Validation Check": "If Flashbots’ builder disappeared, validator block economics and MEV flow would materially change, forcing rapid migration to alternative builders.", "Practitioner’s Note": "Flashbots’ importance is not just market share but norm-setting; many builder and relay patterns follow its architectural decisions.", "Primary MEV Types Enabled": "Arbitrage, liquidations, backrunning, bundle-based MEV", "Protocol Influence Surface": "High (PBS norms, MEV-Boost adoption, ecosystem coordination)", "Reason for Inclusion": "- Constructs full Ethereum blocks\n- Directly influences transaction ordering\n- Operates MEV infrastructure at the protocol boundary", "Single-Point-of-Failure Risk": "High (dominant builder infrastructure)", "Transaction Ordering Control": "Full (within builder pipeline constraints)", "Validator Access Path": "Relay-mediated (primarily via Flashbots Relay; also hybrid relationships)", "Vertical Integration Flag": "Yes (builder + relay + research)"}, "source_label": "MEV & Block Builders"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();
